WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
Then I think there's a reasonable thing that you can think, which is

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:08.000
Should you stay on that project or should you go?

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:14.000
If you spot that a project has got so many different

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:20.000
wild and scary bets that it's got no chance of succeeding at all

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:29.000
What should you do about that? Should you stay? Or should you go? And I think it's legitimate in those kinds of situations. Again, this is something that I've tried to like

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:35.000
take have a different take on kind of a lot of project management books.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:37.000
Is

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:48.000
That not all projects succeed. That's one of the kind of important aspects of looking at projects in terms of bets. And so if you do look at

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:53.000
projects in terms of bets, you realize that some projects are going to fail. And

00:00:53.000 --> 00:01:09.000
Some of the people who are associated with that project are going to be exercising their right to play heads I win, tails you lose, and be around when the project succeeds and not around when the project fails. And there's no reason why you can't do the same

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:15.000
There's no reason why you can't think, well, this project's not going to work out. So you can go somewhere else.

